#: ../../../contributing.md:1
msgid "Contributing to Gazebo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:3
msgid "Thank you for your interest in contributing to Gazebo!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:5
msgid ""
"The following is a set of guidelines for contributing to Gazebo and its "
"components, which are hosted in the [Gazebo Organization](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim) on GitHub. These are mostly guidelines, not rules. Use your best "
"judgment, and feel free to propose changes to this document in a pull "
"request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:11
msgid "Code of Conduct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:13
msgid ""
"This project and everyone participating in it is governed by the [Gazebo "
"Code of Conduct](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/main/"
"CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). By participating, you are expected to uphold this code. "
"Please report unacceptable behavior at [https://gazebosim.org/support]"
"(https://gazebosim.org/support)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:17
msgid "Project Design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:19
msgid "Repository List"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:21
msgid ""
"The following is a list of the major Gazebo repositories. A complete list "
"can be found at [https://github.com/gazebosim/](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:25
msgid ""
"[gz-cmake](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-cmake): CMake modules used to "
"configure and build Gazebo libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:27
msgid ""
"[gz-common](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-common): Set of general purpose "
"components and utilities, such as 3D mesh processing, console logging, and "
"signal handling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:30
msgid ""
"[gz-fuel-tools](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-fuel-tools): Interact with "
"Gazebo Fuel servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:32
msgid ""
"[gz-sim](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim): A high-fidelity 3D rigid-body "
"dynamic simulator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:34
msgid ""
"[gz-gui](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-gui): QT-based library to configure "
"and manage graphical applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:36
msgid ""
"[gz-launch](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-launch): Launch executables and "
"plugins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:38
msgid ""
"[gz-math](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-math): A math library targeted "
"toward robotic applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:40
msgid ""
"[gz-msgs](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-msgs): Protobuf messages and "
"utilities for simulation and robotics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:42
msgid ""
"[gz-physics](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-physics): Plugin based library "
"for physics simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:44
msgid ""
"[gz-plugin](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-plugin): Library for "
"registering, loading, and managing plugin libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:46
msgid ""
"[gz-rendering](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-rendering): Library that "
"supports rendering through different engines, such as [OGRE](https://www."
"ogre3d.org/) and [Optix](https://developer.nvidia.com/optix)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:49
msgid ""
"[gz-sensors](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sensors): A set of models that "
"generate realistic sensor data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:51
msgid ""
"[gz-tools](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-tools): Provides the `gz` command "
"line interface that can be configured and used by multiple libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:54
msgid ""
"[gz-transport](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-transport): High performance "
"inter- and intra-process communication based on [ZeroMQ](http://zeromq.org/) "
"and [Protobuf](https://developers.google.com/protocol-buffers/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:57
msgid ""
"[gz-utils](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-utils): General purpose classes "
"and functions with minimal dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:59
msgid "[sdformat](https://github.com/osrf/sdformat): World description format."
msgstr ""

