#: ../../../contributing.md:67
msgid "How to Contribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:69
msgid "Reporting Bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:71
msgid "**Before Submitting a Bug Report**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:73
msgid ""
"Check the [questions and answers forum](http://answers.gazebosim.org). Your "
"issue may have already been resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:74
msgid ""
"Determine [the repository](contributing.md#repository-list) which should "
"receive the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:75
msgid ""
"Search the repository's issues to see if the same or similar problem has "
"been opened. If it has and the issue is still open, then add a comment to "
"the existing issue. Otherwise, create a new issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:79
msgid "**How to Submit a Good Bug Report**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:81
msgid ""
"Create an issue on the repository that is related to your bug, explain the "
"problem, and include additional details to help maintainers reproduce the "
"problem. Refer to the [Short, Self Contained, Correct (Compilable), Example "
"Guide](http://sscce.org/) as well as the following tips:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:86
msgid ""
"**Use a clear and descriptive title** for the issue to identify the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:87
msgid ""
"**Describe the exact steps which reproduce the problem** in as many details "
"as possible. When listing steps, don't just say what you did, but explain "
"how you did it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:88
msgid ""
"**Provide specific examples to demonstrate the steps.** Include links to "
"files or projects, or copy/pasteable snippets, which you use in those "
"examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:89
msgid ""
"**Describe the behavior you observed after following the steps** and point "
"out what exactly is the problem with that behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:90
msgid "**Explain which behavior you expected to see instead and why**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:91 ../../../contributing.md:145
msgid ""
"**Include screenshots and animated GIFs** which show you following the "
"described steps and clearly demonstrate the problem. See [Creating GIFs]"
"(contributing.md#creating-gifs) for GIF creation utilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:92
msgid ""
"**If the problem wasn't triggered by a specific action**, describe what you "
"were doing before the problem happened and share more information using the "
"guidelines below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:94
msgid "Provide more context by answering these questions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:96
msgid ""
"**Did the problem start happening recently** (e.g. after updating to a new "
"version) or was this always a problem?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:97
msgid ""
"If the problem started happening recently, **can you reproduce the problem "
"in an older version?** What's the most recent version in which the problem "
"doesn't happen?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:98
msgid ""
"**Can you reliably reproduce the issue?** If not, provide details about how "
"often the problem happens and under which conditions it normally happens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:99
msgid ""
"If the problem is related to working with files, **does the problem happen "
"for all files and projects or only some?** Does the problem happen only when "
"working with local or remote files, with files of a specific type (e.g. only "
"Collada or SDF), or with large files or files with very long lines? Is there "
"anything else special about the files you are using?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:101
msgid "Include details about your configuration and environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:103
msgid "**Which version of Gazebo are you using**?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:104
msgid "**What's the name and version of the OS you're using**?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:105
msgid ""
"**Are you running Gazebo in a virtual machine?** If so, which VM software "
"are you using and which operating systems and versions are used for the host "
"and the guest?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:107
msgid "Suggesting Enhancements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:109
msgid ""
"This section guides you through submitting an enhancement suggestion, "
"including completely new features and minor improvements to existing "
"functionality. Following these guidelines helps maintainers and the "
"community understand your suggestion and find related suggestions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:114
msgid ""
"Before creating enhancement suggestions, please check [this list]"
"(contributing.md#before-submitting-an-enhancement-suggestion) as you might "
"find out that you don't need to create one. When you are creating an "
"enhancement suggestion, please [include as many details as possible]"
"(contributing.md#how-do-i-submit-a-good-enhancement-suggestion). When "
"filling in the issue form for an enhancement suggestion, include the steps "
"that you imagine you would take if the feature you're requesting existed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:123
msgid "Before Submitting An Enhancement Suggestion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:125
msgid ""
"**Check if you're using the latest software version**. A more recent version "
"may contain your desired feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:126
msgid ""
"**Check if there's already [a library](https://gazebosim.org/libs) which "
"provides that enhancement.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:127
msgid ""
"**Determine [which repository the enhancement should be suggested in]"
"(contributing.md#repository-list).**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:128
msgid ""
"**Perform a [cursory search](https://github.com/search?"
"q=org%3Agazebosim&type=Issues)** to see if the enhancement has already been "
"suggested. If it has, add a comment to the existing issue instead of opening "
"a new one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:129
msgid ""
"**Ask on the [community forum](https://community.gazebosim.org) about your "
"feature.** Someone else might already have started, and you might be able to "
"help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:133
msgid "How Do I Submit A (Good) Enhancement Suggestion?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:135
msgid ""
"Enhancement suggestions are tracked as [GitHub issues](https://help.github."
"com/en/github/managing-your-work-on-github/about-issues). After you've "
"determined [which repository](contributing.md#repository-list) your "
"enhancement suggestion is related to, create an issue on that repository and "
"provide the following information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:141
msgid ""
"**Use a clear and descriptive title** for the issue to identify the "
"suggestion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:142
msgid ""
"**Provide a step-by-step description of the suggested enhancement** in as "
"many details as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:143
msgid ""
"**Provide specific examples to demonstrate the steps**. Include copy/"
"pasteable snippets which you use in those examples, as [Markdown code blocks]"
"(https://help.github.com/en/github/writing-on-github/creating-and-"
"highlighting-code-blocks)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:144
msgid ""
"**Describe the current behavior** and **explain which behavior you expected "
"to see instead** and why."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:146
msgid ""
"**Explain why this enhancement would be useful** to most users and isn't "
"something that can or should be implemented as a separate application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:147
msgid "**Specify which version of Gazebo you're using.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:148
msgid "**Specify the name and version of the OS you're using.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:150
msgid "Contributing Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:152
msgid ""
"We follow a development process designed to reduce errors, encourage "
"collaboration, and make high quality code. Review the following to get "
"acquainted with this development process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:156
msgid ""
"**Read the [Reporting Bugs](contributing.md#reporting-bugs) and [Suggesting "
"Enhancements](contributing.md#suggesting-enhancements)** sections first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:158
msgid ""
"**Fork the Gazebo library** you want to contribute to. This will create your "
"own personal copy of the library. All of your development should take place "
"in your fork."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:161
msgid ""
"An important thing to do is create a remote pointing to the [upstream remote "
"repository](https://docs.github.com/en/github/collaborating-with-issues-and-"
"pull-requests/configuring-a-remote-for-a-fork). This way, you can always "
"check for modifications on the original repository and **always** keep your "
"fork repository up to date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:163
msgid "**Choose a base branch.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:164
msgid ""
"If your changes will break API or ABI, then base your new branch off of "
"`main`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:165
msgid ""
"If you are making interdependent changes to multiple repositories without "
"breaking API or ABI, it is also recommended to base your new branches off of "
"`main` to simplify automated testing of the changes and the review process. "
"Your changes may be backported to an existing release once all the changes "
"have been merged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:170
msgid ""
"If your changes don't break API/ABI and you would like them to be released "
"to an existing release with major version `N`, then use branch `gz-"
"<library>N` as the base."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:174
msgid ""
"**Work out of a branch** Always work out of a new branch, one that is not a "
"release / main branch. This is a good habit to get in, and will make your "
"life easier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:178
msgid "**Write your code.** This is the fun part, but is good to remember:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:179
msgid ""
"Always [signoff on your commits](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/"
"managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/managing-repository-settings/"
"managing-the-commit-signoff-policy-for-your-repository#about-commit-"
"signoffs) (See the bullet about Developer Certificate of Origin in the "
"[Process](contributing.md#process) section below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:180
msgid ""
"Look at the existing code and try to maintain the existing style and pattern "
"as much as possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:181
msgid "**Always** keep your branch updated with the original repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:183
msgid ""
"**Write tests.** In most cases, a pull request will only be accepted if it "
"has tests. See the [Writing Tests](contributing.md#writing-tests) section "
"below for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:187
msgid ""
"**Resolve compiler warnings.** Code must have zero compile warnings, or at "
"least make sure your pull request is not adding new warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:189
msgid "**Follow the [style guide](contributing.md#style-guides).**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:191
msgid ""
"Static code checking analyzes your code for bugs, such as potential memory  "
"leaks, and style. Most Gazebo libraries use the `cppcheck` static code  "
"checker, and a modified version `cpplint`. Ubuntu  users can install via:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:196
msgid " sudo apt-get install cppcheck\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:198
msgid ""
"To check your code, run the following script from the `build` folder of the "
"project that you're working on.  If you're working on *gz-math*, for "
"instance, the path for the folder should be something similar to `~/"
"citadel_ws/build/gz-math6`.  The path example is assuming you followed [our "
"installation instructions](install) using colcon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:202
msgid "Then, run the script inside this folder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:204
msgid " make codecheck\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:206
msgid ""
"This may take a few minutes to run. Fix all errors and warnings until  the "
"output looks like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:209
msgid " Built target codecheck\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:211
msgid ""
"The tool does not catch all style errors. See the [code style](contributing."
"md#style-guides) section below for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:213
msgid "**(optional) Use clang-tidy for additional checks.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:215
msgid "clang-tidy should return no errors when run against the code base."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:217
msgid "Ubuntu users can install via:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:219
msgid " sudo apt-get install clang-tidy-6.0 libclang-6.0-dev python-yaml\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:221
msgid "clang-tidy can then be executed by running from the source dir:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:223
msgid " ./tools/clang_tidy.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:225
msgid "Address issues that are found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:227
msgid ""
"If you are feeling adventurous, you can experiment with adding additional "
"checks to the `.clang-tidy` file by referencing the full list of options in "
"the [clang-tidy documentation](http://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/"
"list.html)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:229
msgid ""
"**Tests must pass.** You can check by running `make test` in  your build "
"directory. Running tests may take a bit of time, be patient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:232
msgid ""
"**Write documentation.** Document all your code. Every class, function, "
"member variable must have doxygen comments. All code in source files must "
"have documentation that describes the functionality. This will help "
"reviewers and future developers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:234
msgid ""
"**Review your code.** Before submitting your code through a pull request, "
"take some time to review everything line-by-line. The review process will go "
"much faster if you make sure everything is perfect before other people look "
"at your code.  There is a bit of the human-condition involved here. Folks "
"are less likely to spend time reviewing your code if it's sloppy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:240
msgid "**Make small pull requests**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:242
msgid ""
"A large pull request is hard to review, and will take a long time. It is  "
"worth your time to split a large pull request into multiple smaller pull  "
"requests. For reference, here are a few examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:246
msgid "[Small, very nice](https://github.com/osrf/gazebo/pull/2789)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:248
msgid "[Medium, still okay](https://github.com/osrf/gazebo/pull/2784)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:250
msgid "[Too large](https://github.com/osrf/gazebo/pull/2776)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:252
msgid ""
"**Submit a pull request** to the Gazebo library through GitHub when you're "
"ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:254
msgid "**Check Continuous integration**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:256
msgid ""
"The moment you make a pull request, a few test jobs  will be started. These "
"jobs will build your branch on Linux, Mac and  Windows, run all tests and "
"check for warnings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:260
msgid ""
"Check the [Continuous Integration guide](ci)  for information on how to "
"interpret the results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:263
msgid ""
"**Respond to reviewers.** At least two other people have to approve your "
"pull request before it can be merged. Please be responsive to any questions "
"and comments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:265
msgid ""
"**Done, phew.** Once you have met all the requirements, your code will be "
"merged. Thanks for improving Gazebo!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:267
msgid "Tracking Progress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:269
msgid ""
"Gazebo development progress is tracked publicly using a GitHub project "
"board. Using project boards ensures the community has visibility to what’s "
"coming up, external contributors can understand where they can help, and the "
"reasoning behind development decisions are visible to everyone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:274
msgid ""
"Contributors should look at the [\"Core development\" board](https://github."
"com/orgs/gazebosim/projects/3), though it's possible we may have other "
"boards in our organization at various times."
msgstr ""

