msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:312
msgid "Board Columns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:314
msgid "The project board columns are defined below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:316
msgid "**Inbox**: New issues and pull requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:317
msgid "**To do**: Issues ready to be worked on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:318
msgid ""
"**In progress**: Issues being worked on / pull requests being iterated on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:319
msgid "**In review**: Pull requests under review / issues requesting feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:320
msgid "**Done**: Closed issues / pull requests (cleared from time to time)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:322
msgid ""
"If a ticket is not on the board, it means that the core team is not planning "
"to work on it, but the community is welcome to do so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:325
msgid "Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:327
msgid "All Gazebo team members actively:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:329
msgid ""
"**Watch** all Gazebo repositories to receive email notifications of new "
"issues / pull requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:330
msgid "Provide **feedback** to issues as soon as possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:331
msgid "**Review** pull requests as soon as possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:333
msgid "Team members can review pull requests already under review or approved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:334
msgid "Team members can provide some feedback without doing a full review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:336
msgid "During weekly simulation meetings, the team:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:338
msgid "Discusses the **Done** column and archives all tickets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:339
msgid ""
"Discusses the **In Review** column and makes sure all pull requests have "
"reviewers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:340
msgid "Discusses the **In Progress** column"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:341
msgid "Quickly **triages** the inbox, if there’s anything left in it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:343
msgid ""
"If we won’t work on an issue in the near future, **remove** it from the "
"board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:344
msgid ""
"If we think the issue should be tackled, label it **[help wanted](https://"
"github.com/search?"
"q=org%3Agazebosim+label%3A%22help+wanted%22&state=open&type=Issues)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:345
msgid ""
"If we’re going to work on an issue, move it to **To Do**, no assignment "
"necessary initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:346
msgid "If we won’t review a pull request in the near future, **close** it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:348
msgid "When opening a pull-request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:350
msgid ""
"**Labels** according to the targeted collection(s) (blueprint, citadel, etc) "
"will be added automatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:351
msgid "Add yourself as the **assignee**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:353
msgid "Maintainers of each repo will be also automatically assigned"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:355
msgid ""
"It will be automatically triaged to the “Core development” **project board**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:356
msgid "Add **reviewers** as appropriate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:358
msgid ""
"If reviewers won’t be able to review soon, they can remove themselves and "
"also let the original author know"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:360
msgid "Pull requests can be merged when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:362
msgid "They have at least 1 approval from a member of the core team"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:363
msgid "There are no unresolved comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:364
msgid "CI is passing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:365
msgid ""
"[Developer Certificate of Origin](https://developercertificate.org/) (DCO) "
"check is passing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:367
msgid ""
"DCO is a declaration of ownership, basically saying that you created the "
"contribution and that it is suitable to be covered under an open source "
"license (not proprietary)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:368
msgid ""
"All you have to do is end your commit message with `Signed-off-by: Your Full "
"Name <your.name@email.com>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:369
msgid ""
"If your `user.name` and `user.email` configurations are set up in git, then "
"you can simply run `git commit -s` to have your signature automatically "
"appended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:372
msgid "Merging strategy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:374
msgid ""
"For internal contributions, give the original author some time to hit the "
"merge button themselves / check directly with them if it’s ok to merge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:375
msgid "Default to “squash and merge”"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:376
msgid ""
"Review the pull request title and reword if necessary since this will be "
"part of the commit message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:377
msgid ""
"Make sure the commit message concisely captures the core ideas of the pull "
"request and contains all authors' signatures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:378
msgid ""
"“Rebase and merge” when moving files (do a `git mv` as a separate commit)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:379
msgid ""
"“Create a merge commit” when porting changes forward. \"Rebase and merge\" "
"when porting backwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:380
msgid ""
"Refrain from force-pushing while the PR is under review (which includes "
"rebasing and squashing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:382
msgid "Porting changes across branches:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:384
msgid ""
"Pull requests should target the latest [supported version](releases) where "
"the changes can be added in a backwards-compatible way (no API / ABI / "
"behavior break in released branches)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:387
msgid ""
"To backport a pull request (i.e. from a higher version to a lower version), "
"use `git cherry-pick` instead of `git merge`, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:390
msgid ""
"  git checkout gz-<library>N\n"
"  git pull\n"
"  git checkout gz-<library>M\n"
"  git pull\n"
"  git checkout -b N_to_M_<date>\n"
"  git cherry-pick <commits from version N>\n"
"  # Fix conflicts\n"
"  git commit -sam\"Backport from N to M\"\n"
"  # Open pull request\n"
"  # Do not squash, rebase instead\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:401
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can use `mergify` to create backports. Go to the original "
"pull request and add a comment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:404
msgid "  @mergifyio backport gz-<library>M\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:406
msgid "where `M` is the version to backport to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:408
msgid ""
"In certain cases when a pull request is merged into an older release branch, "
"a maintainer will **forward-port** changes to newer release branches all the "
"way up to `main`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:411
msgid ""
"See [this list](https://github.com/gazebosim/docs/blob/master/tools/"
"branch_comparisons.md) to check if a branch needs porting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:412
msgid ""
"The merge forward can be done with `git merge` in order to keep the commit "
"history and so it's easier to compare branches. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:415
msgid ""
"  git checkout gz-<library>M\n"
"  git pull\n"
"  git checkout gz-<library>N\n"
"  git pull\n"
"  git checkout -b username/M_to_N_<date> # It's important to do this before "
"`git merge`\n"
"  git merge gz-<library>M\n"
"  # Fix conflicts\n"
"  git commit -sam\"Merge M into N\"\n"
"  # Open pull request\n"
"  # Do not squash or rebase, create a merge commit\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:427
msgid "Writing Tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:429
msgid ""
"Most Gazebo libraries use [GTest](http://code.google.com/p/googletest) for "
"general testing and [QTest](http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qtest.html) for GUI tests. "
"There are a few kinds of tests:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:433
msgid ""
"**Unit tests**: all classes should have corresponding unit tests. These live "
"in the same directory as the source code and are suffixed by `_TEST`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:436
msgid ""
"**Integration tests**: tests which verify how many classes are working "
"together go under the `tests/integration` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:438
msgid ""
"**Regression tests**: tests which fix broken features go under `tests/"
"regression` and are prefixed by the issue number on library's issue tracker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:440
msgid ""
"**Performance tests**: tests that are designed to check performance "
"characteristics, such as CPU or memory usage, go under `tests/performance`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:443
msgid ""
"Before creating a new integration or performance test file, check the "
"current test files. If one closely matches the topic of your new code, "
"simply add a new test function to the file. Otherwise, create a new test "
"file, and write your test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:448
msgid "Test Coverage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:450
msgid ""
"The goal is to achieve 100% line and branch coverage. However, this is not "
"always possible due to complexity, analysis tools misreporting coverage, and "
"time constraints. Try to write as complete of a test suite as possible, and "
"use the coverage analysis tools as guide. If you have trouble writing a test "
"please ask for help in your pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:456
msgid ""
"Gazebo CMake provides build target called `make coverage` that produces a "
"code coverage report. You'll need to have [lcov](http://ltp.sourceforge.net/"
"coverage/lcov.php) and [gcov](https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Gcov.html) "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:459
msgid "In your `build` folder, compile with `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Coverage`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:461 ../../../contributing.md:474
msgid "If using plain cmake:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:463
msgid ""
" cd <path to build directory>\n"
" cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Coverage ..\n"
" make\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:467 ../../../contributing.md:479
msgid "If using a colcon workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:469
msgid ""
" cd <path to colcon workspace>\n"
" colcon build --cmake-args -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Coverage --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:472
msgid "Run a single test, or all the tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:476
msgid ""
"./bin/UNIT_<TestName>_Test   # single test\n"
" make test                   # all tests\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:481
msgid "Run single/specific test:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:483
msgid ""
"colcon test --ctest-args -R <part of test name> --merge-install\n"
"# or\n"
"./build/<package_name>/bin/UNIT_<TestName>_TEST\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:489
msgid "Run all tests for a single package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:491
msgid "colcon test --packages-select <package_name> --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:495
msgid "Run all tests for all packages in the workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:497
msgid "colcon test --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:501
msgid ""
"When using `colcon test`, all test results end up in the `log` directory.  "
"You can check `log/latest_test` to see the latest results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:504
msgid "Make the coverage report"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:506
msgid " make coverage\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:508
msgid "View the coverage report"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:510
msgid " firefox coverage/index.html\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:512
msgid "Sanitizers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:514
msgid ""
"Sanitizers capture very detailed information during runtime about code "
"quality issues and print them to stderr."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:516
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:518
msgid "Install and enable Colcon mixin package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:520
msgid ""
"pip3 install colcon-mixin\n"
"colcon mixin add default https://raw.githubusercontent.com/colcon/colcon-"
"mixin-repository/master/index.yaml\n"
"colcon mixin update default\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:526
msgid "Install colcon-sanitizer-reports (Recommended):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:528
msgid ""
"git clone https://github.com/colcon/colcon-sanitizer-reports.git\n"
"cd colcon-sanitizer-reports\n"
"sudo python3 setup.py install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:534
msgid ""
"You can find more details [here](https://github.com/colcon/colcon-sanitizer-"
"reports/blob/master/README.rst) about the installation process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:536
msgid "Compiling the code and running the tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:538
msgid ""
"Create a Gazebo workspace for ASAN/TSAN related tasks. Refer to the "
"[official documentation to get all the Gazebo sources](install_ubuntu_src."
"md#getting-the-sources)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:541
msgid "First, compile all packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:543
msgid "ASan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:544
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace  # you will need to be exactly in this directory\n"
"colcon build --build-base=build-asan --install-base=install-asan \\\n"
"    --cmake-args -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \\\n"
"    --mixin asan-gcc\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:551
msgid "TSan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:552
msgid ""
"# Equivalent command for tsan:\n"
"# You can either use different workspaces or the same one.\n"
"colcon build --build-base=build-tsan --install-base=install-tsan \\\n"
"    --cmake-args -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \\\n"
"    --mixin tsan\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:560
msgid ""
"**IMPORTANT:** Do not forget to pass ``-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug`` to ensure "
"that debugging symbols are generated. This allows ASAN/TSAN to report files "
"and line numbers in backtraces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:564
msgid ""
"Once the compilation is finished, colcon will report that all packages have "
"been compiled but some had “stderr output”. This is fine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:567
msgid "To run the tests for ASan:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:568
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace  # you will need to be exactly in this directory\n"
"colcon test --build-base=build-asan --install-base=install-asan \\\n"
"    --event-handlers sanitizer_report+\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:574
msgid "To run tests for TSan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:575
msgid ""
" cd ~/workspace  # you will need to be exactly in this directory\n"
"colcon test --build-base=build-tsan --install-base=install-tsan \\\n"
"  --event-handlers sanitizer_report+\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:581
msgid ""
"Omit the `--event-handlers` flag if you did not install colcon-sanitizer-"
"reports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:583
msgid ""
"Some tests may fail, this is OK. Once done, you can look at the test logs or "
"`sanitizer_report.csv`. Examples from tests logs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:586
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace  # you will need to be exactly in this directory\n"
"cd log/latest_test\n"
"# Displays three lines after the beginning of a ASAN reported issue.\n"
"grep -R '==.*==ERROR: .*Sanitizer' -A 3\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:593
msgid ""
"Review [Appendix - ASAN/TSAN Issues Zoology](https://github.com/colcon/"
"colcon-sanitizer-reports/blob/master/README.rst#appendix---asantsan-issues-"
"zoology) to review which kind of failures you can find in this kind of "
"reports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:596
msgid "Style Guides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:598
msgid ""
"You can check code for compliance by running the following command from a "
"build folder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:601
msgid "    make codecheck\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:603
msgid ""
"In general, we follow [Google's style guide](https://google.github.io/"
"styleguide/cppguide.html) and rules set forth by `cppcheck`. However, we "
"have added some extras listed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:605
msgid "**This pointer**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:606
msgid ""
"All class attributes and member functions must be accessed using the `this-"
">` pointer. Here is an [example](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/"
"de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/src/Server.cc#L89)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:608
msgid "**Underscore function parameters**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:609
msgid ""
"All function parameters must start with an underscore. Here is an [example]"
"(https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/"
"de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/src/Server.cc#L173-L174)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:611
msgid "**Do not cuddle braces**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:612
msgid ""
"All braces must be on their own line. Here is an [example](https://github."
"com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/src/"
"Server.cc#L245-L253)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:614
msgid "**Multi-line code blocks**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:615
msgid ""
"If a block of code spans multiple lines and is part of a flow control "
"statement, such as an `if`, then it must be wrapped in braces. Here is an "
"[example](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/"
"de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/src/Server.cc#L295-L299)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:617
msgid "**++ operator**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:618
msgid ""
"This occurs mostly in `for` loops. Prefix the `++` operator, which is "
"[slightly more efficient than postfix in some cases](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/src/"
"EntityComponentManager_TEST.cc#L108)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:620
msgid "**PIMPL/Opaque pointer**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:621
msgid ""
"If you are writing a new class, it must use a private data pointer. Here is "
"an [example](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/"
"de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/include/ignition/gazebo/"
"EntityComponentManager.hh#L682), and you can read more [here](https://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Opaque_pointer)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:623
msgid "**const functions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:624
msgid ""
"Any class function that does not change a member variable should be marked "
"as `const`. Here is an [example](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/"
"de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/include/ignition/gazebo/"
"EntityComponentManager.hh#L453)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:626
msgid "**const parameters**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:627
msgid ""
"All parameters that are not modified by a function should be marked as "
"`const`, except for \"Plain Old Data\" (`int`, `bool`, etc). This applies to "
"parameters that are passed by reference, and pointer. Here is an [example]"
"(https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/"
"de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/include/ignition/gazebo/Model."
"hh#L111-L112)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:629
msgid "**Pointer and reference variables**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:630
msgid ""
"Place the `*` and `&` next to the variable name, not next to the type. For "
"example: `int &variable` is good, but `int& variable` is not. Here is an "
"[example](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/"
"de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/include/ignition/gazebo/Model."
"hh#L96)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:632
msgid "**Camel case**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:633
msgid ""
"In general, everything should use camel case. Exceptions include SDF element "
"names, and protobuf variable names. Here is an [example](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/de5b025968c9cf0cfbfd8a852458482e87c70c6c/include/"
"ignition/gazebo/SdfEntityCreator.hh#L64-L65)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:635
msgid "**Member function names**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:636
msgid ""
"Member functions, including static member functions, must start with a "
"capital letter, and capitalize every word."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:638
msgid "`void MyClass::MyFunction();` : Good"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:640
msgid "`void MyClass::myFunction();` : Bad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:642
msgid "`void MyClass::my_function();` : Bad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:644
msgid "**Free function names**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:645
msgid ""
"Free functions in namespace and global scope must start with a lowercase "
"letter, and capitalize every word thereafter. `void myFunction();` : Good"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:648
msgid "`void MyFunction();` : Bad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:650
msgid "`void my_function();` : Bad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:652
msgid "**Variable names**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:653
msgid ""
"Variables must start with a lower case letter, and capitalize every word "
"thereafter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:655
msgid "`int myVariable;` : Good"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:657
msgid "`int myvariable;` : Bad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:659
msgid "`int my_variable;` : Bad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:661
msgid "**No inline comments**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:662
msgid "`//` style comments may not be placed on the same line as code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:664
msgid "`speed *= 0.44704;  // miles per hour to meters per second` : Bad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:666
msgid "**Accessors must not start with `Get`**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:667
msgid ""
"Member functions granting read access to protected or private data must look "
"like a noun."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:669
msgid "`public: ::ServerConfig ServerConfig() const;` : Allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:671
msgid "`public: ServerConfig GetServerConfig() const;` : Not Allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:673
msgid "**Corner Cases**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:675
msgid ""
"A class name may conflict with an accessor function. For example, "
"`Model(int)` would conflict with a `Model` class. In these cases, try to "
"follow the `Noun` - `By` pattern. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:677
msgid "`ModelByName(const std::string &_name)` : Allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:679
msgid "`ModelById(const int _id)` : Allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:680
msgid ""
"However, if the function does not have a parameter, it may be difficult to "
"use the `Noun` - `By` pattern. In this case, qualifying the name of the "
"class with its namespace should avoid the conflict. For example, if there is "
"class called `Entity` in the `gazebo` namespace and we want to create an "
"accessor called `Entity()`, we can do the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:683
msgid "`public: gazebo::Entity Entity() const;` : Allowed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:685
msgid ""
"A template function that returns a data type may use a stand-alone `Get`. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../contributing.md:687
msgid "`public: template<typename T> T Get();` : Allowed"
msgstr ""

